## Mission description

Expertise France is the French public agency for international technical cooperation. It works alongside partner countries to advise and support them in strengthening their public policies. To this end, the agency designs, coordinates and implements national and regional projects across the main areas of public action:

\- democratic, economic and financial governance;

\- peace, stability and security;

\- climate, biodiversity and sustainable development;

\- health and human development.

In these areas, Expertise France provides project engineering and implementation services for capacity-building initiatives, mobilises French and international technical expertise, and plays a key role in integrating public-sector expertise and private-sector know-how.

## Project or context description

1. **Project description**

The “Support to Democratic Reforms in Jordan” (SDR) project is a programme funded by the European Union and implemented by Expertise France in Jordan since 1 January 2024. It aims to contribute to a more participatory, inclusive and accountable democratic process, in the context of the modernisation of Jordan’s political system following the work of the Royal Committee to Modernize the Political System.

The programme is therefore implemented within a context of institutional and political reform in Jordan, particularly in relation to strengthening civic and political participation, the evolving role of political parties, and strengthening the capacity of representative institutions.

The project has three main objectives:

- to promote the effective participation of young people and women in political and democratic life, notably by strengthening their capacity to participate in decision-making processes and to raise issues affecting their communities;
- to support political parties and political institutions in developing more professional, inclusive and representative organisations capable of responding to the expectations of their members and society;
- to strengthen the capacity of the House of Representatives to exercise its parliamentary functions with greater professionalism, effectiveness, inclusiveness and accountability.

The interventions cover, in particular, capacity-building and participation of young people and women, dialogue between citizens, political representatives and public institutions, support to political and electoral institutions, strengthening of political parties and inter-party dialogue, as well as strengthening the functions of the House of Representatives, including legislative functions, budgetary oversight and oversight of government action. A cross-cutting component also focuses on communication, outreach and media engagement, with the aim of strengthening citizens’ access to information and participation.

A multi-partner implementation framework

The SDR programme is implemented through a multi-partner framework, bringing together Expertise France, several implementing partners and a wide range of Jordanian stakeholders. The programme is implemented in close coordination with key Jordanian institutions, including the Ministry of Planning and International Cooperation (MoPIC), the Ministry of Political and Parliamentary Affairs (MoPPA), the Independent Election Commission (IEC) and the House of Representatives (HoR). It also involves political parties, civil society organisations, young people and women engaged in civic and political life, as well as the media.

Expertise France works in particular with three implementing partners:

- Netherlands Institute for Multiparty Democracy (NIMD), mainly involved in areas relating to youth political participation, strengthening political parties, inter-party dialogue and support to political institutions;
- Westminster Foundation for Democracy (WFD), mainly involved in strengthening the capacities of the House of Representatives, its committees and services, as well as parliamentary and legislative oversight functions;
- Canal France International (CFI), involved in areas relating to media, civic and political participation, and the role of the media in the democratic process.

The EU also supports a related programme implemented with UN Women, alongside other partners and stakeholders depending on the activities concerned.

Given the diversity of actors involved, Expertise France plays a central role in the coordination and overall management of the programme. The Project Lead ensures the overall coherence of interventions, facilitates synergies between the different partners, maintains dialogue with Jordanian authorities and ensures their information and involvement in programme implementation, as well as their participation in validation processes where necessary. The Project Lead also manages the relationship with the European Union, oversees implementation and results, and represents the programme vis-à-vis key stakeholders.

The project is now entering its final implementation phase, with a No-Cost Extension currently under negotiation with the European Union, with the objective of extending implementation until mid-2027. In parallel, the prospects for a potential second phase are currently being explored with the donor. This period requires close management to secure the implementation of remaining activities, monitor partners, achieve the expected results and ensure the effective use of available resources.

Against this background, Expertise France is recruiting a Project Lead to ensure the overall management of the project, its strategic and operational coherence, and coordination with partners, Jordanian institutions and the European Union.

**2. Position description**

Reporting to the Jordan Portfolio Manager, the Project Lead is responsible for the strategic, operational and administrative management of the SDR project.

The Project Lead ensures effective project implementation, monitors the achievement of results and indicators, coordinates partners and stakeholders, and ensures compliance with the contractual commitments towards the donor. He/she works closely with implementing partners, Jordanian institutions, the European Union Delegation, Expertise France teams and other relevant stakeholders within the ecosystem. In this capacity, he/she plays a central interfacing and coordination role between these different actors.

The position requires strong project management expertise as well as solid knowledge of democratic governance and institutional reform, together with a good understanding of Jordan’s political and institutional context.

2.1 Project management and contractual relations with the European Union

The Project Lead:

- oversees the overall management of the project, its work plan and implementation schedule, and ensures coherence across its different components;
- monitors implementation progress, results, logical framework indicators and key risks, and proposes appropriate corrective measures;
- identifies challenges, delays, risks and potential deviations from project objectives and proposes corrective measures;
- analyses developments in the political and institutional context and their implications for project implementation;
- ensures, in coordination with support teams, financial and budget monitoring and consistency between activities, budget and forecasts;
- prepares and follows up on project governance bodies, including Steering and Technical Committees;
- ensures the relationship with the European Union Delegation in Jordan in relation to the project and is responsible for project reports and deliverables;
- organises and facilitates regular monitoring meetings with the partners;
- ensures the follow-up of any No-Cost Extensions and other contractual adjustments;
- ensures compliance with Expertise France procedures and donor rules.

2.2 Coordination of partners and the Jordanian ecosystem

The Project Lead coordinates the different actors involved in the project and ensures the coherence of their interventions. In this capacity, he/she:

- monitors the implementation of activities by implementing partners, including their work plans, schedules, deliverables and contractual commitments;
- ensures regular administrative and financial monitoring of partnership agreements, in coordination with Expertise France support functions;
- analyses partners’ disbursement and budget execution levels against activity progress, forecasts and contractual timelines;
- identifies discrepancies between forecasts and actual implementation, including activity delays, delayed disbursements and risks of underspending or overspending, and proposes appropriate corrective measures;
- organizes regular follow-up meetings with partners to review progress, challenges and corrective actions;
- ensures complementarity and synergies between the interventions of different partners;
- maintains regular dialogue with relevant Jordanian institutions, ensuring their information, involvement and ownership of activities and, where necessary, their participation in validation processes;
- develops and maintains working relationships with key actors in the democratic governance ecosystem in Jordan and ensure appropriate coordination with other relevant initiatives;
- represents Expertise France and the project vis-à-vis authorities, partners and other stakeholders, including in high-level settings;
- draws on his/her knowledge of Jordan’s political and institutional context to facilitate dialogue between different stakeholders and inform project orientations;
- monitors political and institutional developments that may affect project implementation and analyse their implications.

2.3 Capitalisation and support to project development

- organises and contributes to capitalisation and lessons-learned exercises on project results and experiences;
- contributes to the dissemination and promotion of project results and compliance with donor visibility requirements;
- participates in cross-cutting activities of the Jordan Office and contributes to knowledge-sharing within Expertise France;
- contributes, in coordination with the Portfolio Manager and Headquarters teams, to identifying development opportunities for Expertise France in Jordan, in particular the potential second phase of the project.

2.4 Project team management

The Project Lead:

- manages and supports the project team based in Amman, composed of a Project Officer and a Project Assistant;
- sets priorities, allocates responsibilities and monitors deadlines and promotes effective information sharing and structuring within the team;
- contributes, in coordination with support functions, to mobilising the resources and expertise required by the project.

## Required profile

1. **Candidate profile**

Education

BA degree in any relevant field.

Professional experience

- At least 15 years of professional experience in international cooperation, development or public policy;
- At least 10 years of experience managing programmes or projects funded by international donors, ideally in democratic governance, institutional reform, political participation or institutional strengthening;
- Proven experience managing multi-stakeholder and multi-partner projects;
- Experience working with the European Union and/or other institutional donors;
- Experience engaging and cooperating with public institutions and senior-level officials.

Technical expertise and knowledge of the context

- Strong expertise in democratic governance, institutional reform and institutional strengthening;
- Good knowledge of Jordan’s political and institutional context, its main institutions and their interactions;
- Good understanding of institutional reform processes and issues relating to political participation, political parties and the functioning of representative institutions;
- Ability to analyse complex political and institutional issues and translate them into operational recommendations;
- Good understanding of international cooperation dynamics and stakeholders in Jordan.

Project management skills

- Strong command of the project management cycle: planning, implementation, results monitoring, risk management, reporting and closure;
- Good knowledge of budgetary and contractual management of donor-funded projects;
- Ability to manage several partners and ensure the coherence of complementary interventions;
- Excellent organisational, analytical and synthesis skills.

Interpersonal skills

- Excellent coordination, communication and negotiation skills;
- Strong interpersonal and diplomatic skills;
- Ability to represent Expertise France with senior institutional officials and international partners;
- Leadership skills and ability to bring stakeholders together and work in a multi-actor environment;
- Autonomy, rigour and ability to work in a changing environment.

Languages

- Fluent English, both written and spoken;
- Fluent Arabic required;
- French is an asset.

Duty station

Amman, Jordan, with occasional travel within Jordan and, where applicable, in the region.

## Additional information

Additional information

- Expected start date: October 2027
- Contract type: Permanent contract
- Salary: Depending on experience
- Documents to be submitted:
CV;
Cover letter;
Three professional references, including email addresses and telephone numbers.

Application deadline: 15/10/2026

Candidates interested in this opportunity are invited to submit their application as soon as possible. Expertise France reserves the right to shortlist candidates before the closing date. If you have not heard from us within three weeks, please consider that your application has not been successful.

The selection process will take place in two stages:

- First stage: a shortlist will be established at the discretion of Expertise France;
- Second stage: shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview by videoconference.

The successful candidate will be supported by Expertise France through an onboarding and training period.

**Deadline for application : 2026/10/15 23:53**

## Mission description

Expertise France is the French international technical assistance agency, created from the merger of the six main French public implementing agencies on 1 January 2015, in order to enhance capacities to mobilize technical expertise, making it possible to address the growing needs of emerging and developing countries more effectively. Under the joint supervision of the Ministry of European and Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Economy, within the AFD GROUP, Expertise France aims at participating in French cooperation and development aid through a wide range of interventions in areas such as sustainable development, economic development, public finances, governance and human rights, social protection and employment, health, and issues of stability, safety and security.

Expertise France is accredited by the European Commission for delegated management (the 'six pillars' audit), which means it can be awarded indirect management of projects and guarantees EF's capacity to successfully implement activities and projects with which it is entrusted, and ensure efficient distribution of administrative, hr and financial management tasks.

## Project or context description

Based in Amman, the Finance Officer reports to the Administrative and Finance Manager (RAF) of the Jordan Office, which is part of the Lebanon/Jordan Country Direction. She/He shares the office project portfolio with the Finance Officer and works with the treasury assistant, the project teams, and the logistics and procurement teams.

The Finance Officer supports the RAF in the running of the Finance department and is the financial focal point for the project teams. She/He ensures the reliability of budget follow-ups, the respect of financial reporting deadlines, the quality of audits and the application of the agency’s financial procedures. She/He directly follows a portfolio of projects and the shared cost centres, and contributes to the preparation of office-wide exercises, especially project reviews.

**Financial and budget follow-up of projects in Jordan:**

· Ensure the Budget Follow-Up (BFU) of the projects in her/his portfolio (updates, consistency checks, sharing on time) according to the agency’s established format;

· Set up the BFUs of new projects in her/his portfolio

· Organise and lead the monthly BFU meetings with the project teams of her/his portfolio;

· Support the RAF in the agency budget exercises (initial budget, revised budget and landing forecasts);

· Prepare the half-year and annual closing of the projects in her/his portfolio (production and check of the Matrix) under the supervision of the RAF;

· Contribute to the reliability of the contractual and financial information available for the projects supported by the USP, especially in Atlas

**Financial reporting & relations with HQ**

· Prepare the financial reports of her/his portfolio and do a first check before sending them to the RAF;

· Keep an updated consolidated calendar of reports and audits for the whole office, in liaison with the RAF, the Finance Officer and the HQ project officers;

· Keep a consolidated status of donor payment requests for the whole office (sent, pending, late), based on the follow-up done by each finance officer;

· Ensure the quality of the reports sent, standard communication, and the respect of HQ and donor deadlines

**Audit management**

· Prepare the external audits of her/his portfolio (ToR, purchase requests, collection of supporting documents, answers to pending issues);

· Coordinate, in liaison with the RAF, communication and exchanges with external auditors for the projects within her/his portfolio;

· Follow up the sending of the final audit reports within the contractual deadlines

**Support to the RAF on the running of the Finance department**

· Contribute to setting up and applying the office monthly financial cycle (closing, sending of accounting documents, controls);

· Take part in sharing the financial procedures with the project teams and help them apply them (expenditure process, reception decision, payment approvals (BAP));

· Identify the difficulties met by the project teams and suggest practice adjustments to the RAF

**Project financial management**

· Directly follow the finances of the most complex projects of the Jordan office portfolio (donor requirements, volume, audit frequency), according to the split decided by the RAF, especially the check and processing of payment files (ATLAS payment vouchers – BAP);

· Be the main financial contact person for the project managers of these projects;

· Follow up the payments (BAP) of the shared cost centres for the operating budgets;

· Ensure consistency between the accounting journals and the treasury journals of the projects and cost centres of her/his portfolio, including the follow up on accounting analytical adjustments in liaison with Headquarters

· Check general and analytical accounting entries (project budget allocations);

· Follow up, with the other departments, the VAT refund and exemption mechanism for the projects of her/his portfolio

**Cross-cutting responsibilities**

· Take part in USP/project coordination meetings;

· Prepare the half-year reviews of all office projects, in liaison with the RAF and the project teams;

· Support the implementation of internal control;

· Support the RAF on communication and payment processes between finance, accounting and treasury

**Archiving:**

· Implement the archiving procedure for her/his finance files;

· Contribute to filing and archiving the Finance department files according to the office filing plan.

## Required profile

**Qualifications, Professional experience and competences**:

· Education: A Bachelor degree in finance /accounting or any related field

· Experience: at least 5 years of experience working with an international NGO or similar organisations

· Sound knowledge of international donors procedures

· Languages: Fluency in written and spoken English and Arabic.

· French is an added value

· Computer skills: Experience in the usage of computers and office software packages (MS Word, Excel, etc.) and knowledge of database package

## Additional information

Candidates interested in this opportunity are invited to submit their application as soon as possible. Expertise France reserves the right to shortlist candidates before the closing date. If you have not heard from us within three weeks, please consider that your application has not been successful.

The selection process will take place in two stages:

\- First stage: a shortlist will be established at the discretion of Expertise France;

\- Second stage: shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview by videoconference.

The successful candidate will be supported by Expertise France through an onboarding and training period.

**Deadline for application : 2026/10/18 23:55**

Rejoindre l’ONG Plan International France, c’est donner un sens à sa vie professionnelle en s’engageant dans la solidarité internationale et en adhérant aux valeurs de transparence, de respect, de durabilité, de communauté et d’inclusion.

Notre ONG est fière d’œuvrer pour un monde meilleur dans lequel les droits des enfants, et en particulier des filles, sont respectés. C’est ainsi qu’en 2025, le réseau Plan International a permis à 5,1 millions de filles dans le monde de bénéficier d’un meilleur accès à l’éducation.

Rejoindre notre ONG, c’est aussi intégrer une équipe conviviale d’une quarantaine de salarié·es et de bénévoles, aussi expert·es que passionné·es. Nous travaillons dans la bienveillance et la confiance, en gardant pour objectif le bien-être des salarié·es. Télétravail, flexibilité des horaires, grande autonomie sont autant d’aménagements qui favoriseront votre équilibre vie pro/vie perso. Vous trouverez une palette de métiers variés et une organisation qui s’inscrit dans une dynamique de progression.

Pour compléter cette belle équipe, nous recherchons des talents qui partagent nos valeurs et qui souhaitent apporter leur pierre à l’édifice. Venez donc nous rencontrer pour découvrir les belles missions qui nous animent et nous motivent.

## **Le poste que nous proposons**

Au sein du département Programmes et partenariats stratégiques et plus spécifiquement du pôle MEESA-APAC (Moyen-Orient, Afrique de l’Est et australe – Asie-Pacifique), la∙le Chargé·e de projets assure le suivi des projets de son portefeuille, de leur démarrage à leur clôture. Il·elle appuie les bureaux terrain pour suivre l’application des standards de qualité de Plan International et la conformité aux exigences des bailleurs de fonds (reporting, suivi bailleur, visites terrain, etc.) en lien avec les autres pôles et départements de Plan International France.

Sous la responsabilité de la Responsable de programmes du pôle MEESA-APAC, la∙le Chargé·e de projets est en charge de :

**Assurer le suivi des projets de son portefeuille :**

Appuyer les bureaux de terrain tout au long du cycle de projet, conformément aux procédures de Plan International et des bailleurs, pour cela :

- Superviser la mise en œuvre des projets de leur démarrage à leur clôture ;
- Suivre la réalisation des indicateurs ;
- Apporter un appui aux bureaux pays pour la réalisation d’activités stratégiques (notamment celles définies dans le FAD) liées au portefeuille de projets (ateliers, évaluations internes et externes, revues après actions, mise en œuvre du cadre qualité, capitalisation, communication, COPIL, partenariat) ;
- S’assurer de la conformité contractuelle et budgétaire du portefeuille des projets avec l’appui du pôle Conformité et Finances des programmes (y compris pour assurer la cohérence entre le reporting opérationnel et le reporting financier) ;
- Assurer le suivi des exigences des bailleurs et/ou mécènes sur son portefeuille de projets, et assurer le rôle de point focal bailleur lorsque cela est pertinent ;
- Assurer des visites régulières de suivi des projets ;
- Assurer le rapportage des activités et des dépenses des budgets aux bailleurs selon le calendrier de rapportage des projets ;
- Établir et suivre le calendrier de rapportage des projets.

**Assurer la coordination générale de projets spécifiques, le cas échéant**

- Coordonner la mise en œuvre générale de projets, en lien avec les équipes concernées du/des CO et de Plan International France ;
- Suivre et piloter la réalisation des indicateurs ;
- Coordonner les activités transversales ou de pilotage du projet, en lien avec le/les CO (ateliers, évaluations internes et externes, capitalisation, communication, COPIL, partenariat) ;
- S’assurer de la conformité contractuelle et budgétaire du portefeuille des projets avec l’appui du pôle Conformité et Finances ;
- Assurer des visites régulières de suivi des projets ;
- Assurer le rapportage des activités et des dépenses des budgets aux bailleurs.

**Apporter un appui transversal aux programmes (zone géographique MEESA-APAC)**

- Assurer le suivi des documents relatifs aux projets dans sa zone et l’archivage des documents pour la bonne circulation des informations entre les différents pôles/départements ;
- Soutenir le·la Responsable Programmes sur d’autres missions transverses : documentation, recherche, études ;
- Appuyer le·la Responsable Programmes pour le montage de projets ;
- Apporter des contributions au·à la Responsable Programmes dans la réflexion stratégique et à la définition des plans d’action annuels.

**Apporter un appui transverse au département Programmes et à Plan International France**

- Appuyer la mise en œuvre de dossiers transversaux de l’équipe programmes ;
- Participer aux réunions d’équipe et être force de proposition pour atteindre les objectifs communs ;
- Assurer un bon partage de l’information sur les projets de son portefeuille avec les autres pôles et départements ;
- Participer à des chantiers transversaux avec les autres pôles et départements ;
- Participer à des groupes de travail avec d’autres ONGs ;
- Assurer le rôle de point focal sur une ou plusieurs thématiques d’intervention de l’ONG.

## **Le profil que nous cherchons**

Vous êtes diplômé∙e d’un master en gestion de projets, solidarité ou coopération internationale. Vous disposez de trois ans d’expérience minimum dont une expérience de terrain significative. La connaissance des zones d’intervention est un plus.

Également:

- Excellente maitrise de la gestion du cycle de projets ;
- Connaissance de la gestion des contrats de subvention des bailleurs publics bilatéraux et multilatéraux (AFD est un plus) ;
- Expérience de la relation partenariale dans le milieu de la coopération internationale ;
- Intérêt pour le développement de partenariats public/privé et du mécénat ;
- Expérience et/ou fort intérêt pour les thématiques liées à l’enfance, l’éducation, l’égalité de genre ;
- Excellentes capacités rédactionnelles ;
- Parfaite maitrise du français et de l’anglais (oral, écrit), l’espagnol (ou le portugais) est un plus ;
- Réactivité, sens de l’organisation et gestion des priorités ;
- Excellentes capacités d’adaptation, y compris dans un environnement multiculturel ;
- Bonnes capacités à résoudre les problèmes de façon autonome ;
- Sens de l’engagement, sens de la diplomatie et de la redevabilité, goût du travail en équipe ;
- Disponibilité pour des déplacements dans les pays d’intervention ;
- Forte adhésion aux valeurs et au mandat de Plan International France

Dans le cadre du programme Better Regional Migration Management (BRMM), l’Organisation internationale pour les migrations (OIM), basée à Djibouti, recrute un consultant national (enquêteur/collecteur de données temporaire) pour une durée de 12,5 jours afin de réaliser la collecte de données auprès des bénéficiaires du programme Youth Business Incubator (YBI). Cette mission s’inscrit dans le cadre d’une étude de suivi visant à évaluer les résultats, les effets et l’impact de l’initiative.

## Contexte et portée du projet

Le programme Better Regional Migration Management (BRMM), intitulé « Mobilité de la main-d’œuvre et intégration régionale pour une migration de travail sûre, ordonnée et humaine en Afrique de l’Est et dans la Corne de l’Afrique », est financé par le Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) du Royaume-Uni.

Ce programme vise à renforcer la gouvernance de la migration de main-d’œuvre ainsi que la protection des travailleurs migrants et des membres de leurs familles. Il favorise la coopération nationale, régionale et transfrontalière afin d’améliorer la mobilité de la main-d’œuvre, de promouvoir le recrutement éthique et de renforcer la protection des droits humains, sociaux et économiques des migrants.

Le programme contribue également à la mise en œuvre des cadres régionaux et internationaux relatifs à la migration, à l’élargissement des voies de migration régulière et à l’intégration régionale, dans une perspective de croissance économique inclusive et durable, tout en favorisant l’autonomisation des jeunes et des femmes.

En mars 2024, l’OIM a organisé un incubateur de jeunes entrepreneurs réunissant des jeunes du Kenya et de l’Ouganda issus de centres de formation technique et professionnelle (TVET). Les participants ont présenté des idées de projets accompagnées de plans d’affaires simplifiés. À l’issue de cette formation intensive d’une semaine, quatre lauréats ont reçu une subvention de démarrage pour lancer leurs activités.

Compte tenu du succès de cette initiative, le programme BRMM a étendu l’activité à neuf pays partenaires, touchant près de 900 jeunes au 31 mai 2026. Afin d’assurer une mise en œuvre harmonisée, deux ateliers régionaux de formation de formateurs ont été organisés à destination des équipes des neuf pays participants.

Cette initiative est désormais considérée comme l’une des activités phares du programme BRMM. Afin d’évaluer sa durabilité et son impact sur les bénéficiaires, l’OIM prévoit la réalisation d’une étude régionale de suivi (tracer study) auprès des jeunes ayant participé au programme Youth Business Incubator (YBI).

## Unité organisationnelle bénéficiaire

**Division Mobilité de la main-d’œuvre et Inclusion sociale (LMI)**

**Programme Better Regional Migration Management (BRMM)**

Description des tâches

### Objectif général de la mission

La mission a pour objectif principal de collecter des données quantitatives et qualitatives fiables, complètes et de qualité auprès des bénéficiaires du programme YBI afin de mesurer les effets et les résultats du projet.

### Responsabilités principales

- Réaliser des entretiens structurés à l’aide du questionnaire standardisé de l’OIM ;
- Garantir l’exactitude, l’exhaustivité et la confidentialité des informations collectées ;
- Respecter les normes éthiques ainsi que les procédures de protection des données de l’OIM ;
- Obtenir le consentement éclairé de tous les participants avant la réalisation des entretiens ;
- Saisir correctement et intégralement les réponses dans les outils de collecte prévus ;
- Participer aux réunions quotidiennes de suivi et de débriefing avec le superviseur ;
- Contribuer à la validation préliminaire et au nettoyage des données collectées ;
- Respecter en tout temps le Code de conduite de l’OIM ainsi que les principes de protection des données.

